84:These are counted overlaps, not prevalence estimates for unscanned files. The final exact-package counts are in [the corrected Rico audit](datasets_scratch/rico_aw_exact_audit.json) and [additional joins](datasets_scratch/additional_rico_audit.json). The earlier broad-name diagnostic `rico_audit.json` includes unrelated recorder apps and must **not** be used as the AW contamination count.
86:**1. GUI-Odyssey — viable new trajectories, with a real conversion cost.** The current release is [HF `hflqf88888/GUIOdyssey`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/hflqf88888/GUIOdyssey/tree/main). Its complete `all_annot.json` index is 2,862,103 bytes and contains **8,334 episodes / 127,893 indexed steps**. The older [OpenGVLab repository card](https://huggingface.co/datasets/OpenGVLab/GUI-Odyssey) describes **7,735 episodes, 201 apps and 118,791 screenshots** and points to the new release; these are versions of a dataset, not two independent corpora. The newer paper reports 212 apps; raw app-label aliases are not a reliable count of distinct packages. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2406.08451), [local index audit](datasets_scratch/odyssey_audit.json).
88:Images are a split ZIP, `screenshots/screenshots.z01` through `.z08` plus `screenshots.zip`, **92,639,510,437 bytes** in total. Annotation JSONs are separately accessible. A ranged sample yielded a real 2208×1840 PNG. Indexed device dimensions include 720×1280, 1080×2400, 1344×2992, 1440×3120, 2560×1600 and both orientations of 2208×1840. Full archive CRC/completeness remains unverified. Raw download works; do not assume `load_dataset()` works from the card's configuration. The downloaded [`splits/random_split.json`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/hflqf88888/GUIOdyssey/blob/main/splits/random_split.json) separates **6,668 train episodes / 102,086 steps** and **1,666 test episodes / 25,807 steps**; use its train IDs for the proposed quota. Other app/task/device splits exist; they are alternate partitions, not extra data. The device split holds out 1,381 tablet episodes. [Split/index join](datasets_scratch/odyssey_split_audit.json).
92:Collection used its own Android emulators; downloaded [episode metadata](datasets_scratch/odyssey_example3.json) records Android 14/API 34, rather than the AW emulator configuration. The full index has app **names**, not package IDs. No exact names of the 14 targets were found, but **8 episodes** mention `Simple Calendar` or `Simple Calendar - easy planner`; quarantine these until their packages are identified. The generic `Calendar` label appears in 421 episodes and needs package resolution or conservative exclusion too; it cannot certify an AW-clean calendar source. Home-screen icons and intermediate unlisted apps are beyond this index check.
94:Human demonstrations are stronger evidence than the subsequently generated GPT-4o instructions, context and SAM2 boxes. Do not use post-hoc context as causal history: an inspected record describes text already entered before the corresponding `TEXT` action. [Issue 19](https://github.com/OpenGVLab/GUI-Odyssey/issues/19) reports 780/25,807 checked cases with dimension-order differences; the author explains that device metadata can differ from rotated screenshots and that normalized coordinates use actual screenshots. That is **not** a demonstrated 3% coordinate-error rate. Older [missing-image reports](https://github.com/OpenGVLab/GUI-Odyssey/issues/16) justify a manifest/CRC check but should not be attributed automatically to the new archive.
98:**2. AMEX — prioritize its 38,709 actual action rows, not its headline element count.** [HF `Yuxiang007/AMEX`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Yuxiang007/AMEX/tree/main) is public. `AMEX/instruction_anno.zip` is **3,105,724 bytes** and was downloaded in full. It contains **3,046 episodes / 38,709 steps**. Its eight image parts plus final ZIP total **93,481,307,584 bytes**; `element_anno.zip` is another **115,510,591 bytes**. The publisher's ~104K screenshots and 110 apps include additional autonomous screen exploration, not 104K demonstrated agent decisions. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2407.17490), [complete annotation audit](datasets_scratch/amex_audit.json).
100:| AMEX released action | Count | Conversion |
110:No long-press action occurs in this released trajectory annotation set. The schema includes `instruction`, `episode_id`, `steps`, `touch_coord`, `lift_coord`, `device_dim`, `package_name`, `type_text`, `need_human_check`, `interest_region`, and `image_path`. Resolutions span 1080×2280, 1080×2400, 1440×2960/3040/3120 and a small landscape tail; a real sampled PNG is 1440×2960. The paper describes AVD/Genymotion collection with Appium, not AW task collection. Scanning **all 38,709 step package fields found zero exact matches to the 14 AW packages**. This finding covers trajectories, not every autonomous screenshot or home-screen icon. `com.google.android.apps.tasks` is not AW's `org.tasks`.
114:The released functionality coverage is materially smaller than a naive reading of the headline ~711K element count. In [the author's issue response](https://github.com/yuxiangchai/AMEX-codebase/issues/2), the author confirms roughly **300K functionality descriptions on ~20K screens** and says this is the full version. Many elements have empty descriptions. Code availability and its licence do not change the data's **CC BY 4.0** card declaration.
116:**USE-WITH-FILTER**: exclude flagged/inconsistent episodes, preserve separate Enter, filter gesture meaning, reject invalid/missing screenshots and unresolved impossible cases, then balance apps and actions. Stronger incremental value than another large pile of synthetic boxes, particularly for typing/Enter/terminal behavior. Estimated **10–18 h**; full media transfer about **2.1 h at an ideal 100 Mbps**. Reuse this image cache if testing Aria or Atlas AMEX labels.
122:The HF card has no explicit data licence or licence file. The linked Microsoft code is MIT; original AC terms are conflicting. The JSON has no app/package fields, so apply the project's existing AW exclusion **after joining back to source episodes**, not merely the train-ID allowlist. **REJECT as an additional v2 source**: it adds neither new screenshots nor full-action supervision, and commercial annotation rights are unresolved. If grounding ablation is needed, reweight original AC low-level click rows first. A later licensed, filtered Actor alternative costs **3–6 h** and no new image download; it should replace, not duplicate, those rows.
128:| `amex_images_part_aa`, `_ab`, `_ac` | 92,099,634,755 bytes combined; AMEX repackaging |
129:| `amex_raw.json` | 327,588,775 bytes; only a bounded prefix was inspected |
136:The [publisher README](https://huggingface.co/datasets/OS-Copilot/OS-Atlas-data/blob/main/README.md) explicitly identifies its AndroidWorld source. The other components predate or are independent of AW collection, but the package joins above prove residual VLC/OsmAnd overlap. UIBert sample imagery is 1080×1920; Rico is mixed original Android dimensions and AMEX retains its higher-resolution source family. Do not assume one fixed resolution from an archive's name.
140:**USE-WITH-FILTER** as a small grounding alternative: remove both AW files, join Rico IDs to packages, enforce source train splits where recoverable, exclude noninteractive/ambiguous targets, select one paraphrase per image/box, and deduplicate against AMEX/Aria/original Widget Captioning. No blanket lossless-conversion or commercially cleared-all-sources claim is justified. Budget **6–12 h**; Rico/UIBert-only media is **7.04 GB**, around nine minutes at ideal 100 Mbps, versus ~2.2 h for all non-AW mobile media/labels. Default mix allocation is zero until a grounding deficit is measured.
142:**5. Aria-UI mobile — a synthetic label expansion of AMEX.** The file is [`Aria-UI/Aria-UI_Data/mobile/aria_ui_mobile_AMEX_1077k.json`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Aria-UI/Aria-UI_Data/tree/main/mobile), **1,632,415,539 bytes**. The publisher describes ~104K AMEX screens and ~1.1M instructions; the filename suggests 1,077K. I inspected a 1 MB prefix containing 47 complete image records, **not all million instructions**. The mobile folder does not provide a new mobile screenshot archive: retrieve the corresponding AMEX images, potentially another 93.48 GB if uncached.
146:The Apache-labelled new annotations retain AMEX image obligations. No AW package fields are present in the inspected Aria records; join back to original AMEX metadata, and do not extend the trajectory-only zero-overlap result to all 104K screens. The [paper's 44.8% AW result](https://arxiv.org/html/2412.16256) uses a GPT-4o planner and an Aria grounder with history; it is not the performance of a small standalone screenshot-only policy. The card's warnings about broken older desktop image mappings concern desktop files, not a demonstrated defect in this mobile file.
148:**USE-WITH-FILTER** for a tightly bounded grounding ablation, not a million-row addition. Estimated **6–12 h** once AMEX is cached; annotation-only transfer roughly two minutes at ideal 100 Mbps. Default allocation **zero** because the recommended mix already uses AMEX and because original AC provides grounding supervision. If selected, replace 2–4K rows, rather than counting AMEX, Atlas-AMEX and Aria-AMEX as three diverse sources.
152:**ScreenQA.** The real host is [`google-research-datasets/screen_qa`](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/screen_qa), with `answers_and_bboxes/{train,validation,test}.json` and `short_answers/{train,validation,test}.json`. Full train labels are **20,193,256 bytes**; short train labels **8,681,944 bytes**. The release has 85,984 question instances on 35,352 screens: **68,951 / 8,614 / 8,419** questions in train/validation/test. Both answer representations describe the same questions, so they must not be counted as independent samples. The full train metadata has 53,388 rows at 1080×1920, 15,560 at 540×960 and three at 1920×1080; actual image dimensions govern any geometry conversion.
154:Full rows contain `image_id`, width/height, question, and `ground_truth` with `full_answer` plus UI text and pixel bounds. Short answers are generated variants. A question becomes the goal, history is `None`, and a selected grounded answer becomes `{"action_type":"answer","text":"..."}`. This is a good semantic fit for single-screen answering; there is no navigation history or evidence of task completion to synthesize separately. Do not turn answer-text boxes into clicks. Human full answers have stronger provenance than model-generated shortenings; train has fewer independent raters than evaluation. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2209.08199), [explicit dataset licence](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/screen_qa/blob/main/LICENSE).
156:The [black-image issue](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/screen_qa/issues/2) reports screen 37374 with a meaningful Ford-related label but a black image. This is a credible mismatch report, not proof of a corpus-wide error rate. **USE-WITH-FILTER**: original train only, remove the 48 conservative AW-app rows, inspect image/label alignment, exclude answers unreadable after the actual model resize, and choose one short or full answer per question. Estimated **4–8 h** and the shared 6.47 GB media download. Its main value is filling the `answer` behavior gap, not increasing next-click accuracy. Use brief answers especially for 450M.
160:**Screen2Words.** The real host is [`google-research-datasets/screen2words`](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/screen2words), not an assumed HF mirror. `screen_summaries.csv` is **5,313,544 bytes / 112,085 rows**, five human summaries per **22,417** Rico screens. `split/` defines **15,743 train screens / 78,715 train captions**, plus dev/test. Select at most one summary per screen if ever used. The original README/tree contains no explicit licence file or dataset grant located in this audit; a downstream CC BY tag and Google's code-repository Apache licence do not settle it. **REJECT for current v2**, both for unresolved terms and low marginal value compared with direct ScreenQA. Conversion to a broad “describe this screen” answer is possible, but it teaches neither navigation nor precise task-state answers. It shares old Rico media, has the quantified AW-app overlap above, and needs the same image/readability checks. Estimate **3–6 h** if terms are resolved.
164:`nodeId` is a dotted view-hierarchy path, not a coordinate. The README gives the exact traversal from `activity.root` through `children`; join the original Rico JSON to recover the target rectangle, validate alignment, and then normalize. Captions describe purpose and may describe a multi-step effect. Either construct a well-specified region-question answer, or use only instructions that truly identify a clickable target; arbitrary caption-to-click conversion is lossy. No trajectory, completion or infeasibility labels exist. Explicit **CC BY 4.0 annotations** coexist with Rico terms. **USE-WITH-FILTER**: `rc` + original train only, package filter, valid visible node, one paraphrase, verified target semantics. At **8–12 h** from original files, it is a secondary option; Atlas preprocessing lowers adapter cost but requires split provenance checks and deduplication. Default allocation zero.
170:| Microsoft | GUI-Actor above; **GUI-Libra** below; Microsoft-associated **ShowUI** releases desktop/web grounding data, while its mobile training instructions reuse AMEX, GUIAct and AitW. Do not count a separate new ShowUI mobile corpus. [Official training instructions](https://github.com/showlab/ShowUI/blob/main/TRAIN.md), [Microsoft GUI-Libra publication](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/publication/gui-libra-data-efficient-post-training-for-reliable-reasoning-and-acting-in-native-gui-agents/) |
181:**GUI-Libra — useful curation, not 81K independent new demonstrations.** [HF `GUI-Libra/GUI-Libra-81K-SFT`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/GUI-Libra/GUI-Libra-81K-SFT/tree/main) contains multiple coordinate/reasoning variants of the same examples and source-specific image tar parts. Publisher scale is ~81K steps / ~9K trajectories, with a web component; **do not sum four annotation variants**. Image archives total about 161.54 GB: AC 35.61 GB, AMEX 25.67 GB, Odyssey 83.97 GB, plus AitW, Android-in-the-Zoo and web sources. The full downloaded AC annotation variant is 63,039,097 bytes and yields the clean official-train intersection above. Reuse originals instead of its AC media archive.
185:**USE-WITH-FILTER** as an alternative selection of AC/AMEX/Odyssey, not an additive multiplier. Audit every selected source separately; Android-in-the-Zoo does not inherit clearance simply because this mixture says Apache. AW-package joins remain necessary for the AC subset. Default allocation zero because direct sources provide simpler provenance. Expected cost **6–12 h per selected source**, and no distinct measured benefit for these small models has been established.
189:Actual train actions: **76,333 CLICK, 9,873 TYPE, 7,509 STOP, 4,310 SWIPE, 43 LONG_PRESS, 31 KEY_BACK, 54 KEY_HOME, 15 WAIT**. Pixels and screenshot dimensions are explicit. Observed dimensions are mostly 1440×3200 and 1080×2400, with 720×1560/1280 and landscape variants. Click, long-press, text, back/home, wait and genuine STOP can be mapped; swipes have the same loss as AMEX. There is no demonstrated answer/infeasible category. **11,051 episodes lack STOP**, so the last interaction is not a labelled completed-state screenshot.
191:No exact AW-app name appears in the train app-name field; however, `日历` (Calendar), `笔记` (Notes), `Recorder` and generic system names are not package identification. Exclude unresolved generic apps for a strict app-held-out claim. No AC origin is declared, so its local numeric IDs must not be intersected directly with AC IDs. Both CMGUI splits restart episode IDs at zero: the meaningful check instead found **2,148 shared screenshot filenames**, affecting **332 of 386 test episodes**. This proves shared media references, not necessarily identical full trajectories; it makes CMGUI's own nominal train/test separation unsafe without additional filtering. Remove any train episode touching a CMGUI-test filename if retaining that benchmark. [Full audit](datasets_scratch/cmgui_audit.json).
201:Its AitW-General-derived smartphone records include goals, history, pixel and normalized points, and image dimensions: 412×732, 540×1080/1140/1170 and 720×1440/1480/1520. The [paper's action-conversion appendix](https://arxiv.org/html/2406.11317) confirms that Back/Home were converted into taps on the navigation bar; their original action identity is therefore absent. A tap/Enter/type/terminal adapter is simple, but navigation-bar taps require the expected visible buttons, and raw swipes still lose target/distance semantics. Reconstruct causal history rather than blindly trusting formatted histories. No app/package field in these annotation rows permits a comprehensive AW-package count; recover it through AitW episode IDs or exclude unresolved examples. It was not collected as AW rollouts and is not AC-derived. Low resolution and AitW's repeated task templates constrain expected gain, while low download cost and Enter coverage are useful.
203:The official project explicitly declares CC BY 4.0 for datasets; the HF metadata says Apache. Both are permissive but differ in obligations, so retain attribution rather than treating the HF tag as licence erasure. The original AitW-specific data grant was not established in this audit, so commercial clearance of the repackaged source also remains unresolved. **USE-WITH-FILTER** as an 8K-row research replacement for AMEX when transfer/storage costs dominate, with resolved package provenance, genuine terminal mappings and supported gestures. Estimated **6–10 h**, ~six minutes ideal media transfer at 100 Mbps. Do not add its 7,246 markers to an `answer` quota.
207:GZIP TFRecords carry encoded screenshots, dimensions, `current_activity`, episode ID, and actions. Important detail: stored touch/lift fields are **`yx_touch` / `yx_lift`**, i.e. y before x, even though descriptions may discuss x/y points. `DUAL_POINT` combines tap and swipe, and lacks the project's exact scroll semantics; text types into the focused field; back/home/Enter/status have direct equivalents. No factual answer labels. Actual full-release screenshot dimensions and AW-package prevalence were not enumerated in this audit; read the per-record dimensions and package-bearing activity before conversion. Collection predates AW; app overlap can still occur.
209:GoogleApps has very many trajectories but only a few hundred prompt templates. The AMEX paper's sampled reannotation found **93.43% agreement** on a random AitW subset and illustrates errors; that is not proof that 6.57% of all AitW rows are wrong. I did not locate an explicit dataset-specific licence grant in the original README, full paper or bucket listing; the arXiv page's CC BY label licenses the *paper*, and the monorepo Apache licence covers code. Commercial data/model clearance is therefore **unresolved**, not established by a third-party HF mirror.
217:[seq2act](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/seq2act) has public recreated PixelHelp TFRecords (ten files, about **0.075 GB**) and AndroidHowTo annotation pointers. The [PixelHelp README](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/seq2act/blob/master/data/pixel_help/README.md) specifies **187 multi-step instructions**: 88 general, 38 Gmail, 31 Chrome and 30 Photos tasks. Its documented features are UI-object text, geometry, hierarchy and action/target sequences; it does not document encoded screenshot features. The [authors' data-generation notes](https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/seq2act/data_generation) distinguish recreated releases from original experiments where copyright prevented direct release. AndroidHowTo reconstruction requires thousands of ~1–2 GB Common Crawl WARC files; it is not a ready screenshot-action corpus. **REJECT for v2**: this small evaluation resource is not a demonstrated screenshot-only training pool, and source-specific commercial terms/image availability are unresolved. No AW target app is identified by those four task categories, but no package-level payload audit was performed. Investigating a screenshot join would take roughly **4–8 h** before any usable-row commitment; expected incremental value is low for all three target evaluations/model sizes.
227:Records target detection/grounding/pointing, not navigation histories or terminals. Filtering the repackaged OS-Atlas origin could in principle remove AW provenance and retain only mobile references, but that full filtering was not performed. No common resolution can be assumed; source dimensions are required. The README explicitly preserves original licences and requires source terms compliance; a NVIDIA model licence is not the data licence. **REJECT for this v2** because direct filtered Atlas/AMEX/Rico offers the same relevant signal with much less engineering and transfer. Estimated **8–16 h** just to build and check a reliable filtered reader; ~15 h ideal transfer for the OS-Atlas component at 100 Mbps. No independently established label-quality improvement over the upstream source was found.
233:For a further cautionary example outside the requested company list, **Kwai's MobileForge** has a real [public exploration release](https://huggingface.co/datasets/lgy0404/mobileforge-exploration-trajectories): publisher **520 trajectories / 5,839 steps**, 3.70 GB raw plus 2.30 GB parsed assets, Apache card. Its package table contains **all 14 AW apps**. It is generated target-app exploration rather than human demonstrations; the full action/media payload was not inspected. **REJECT** for this held-out-app objective regardless of small download size. It must not be misattributed to Alibaba or treated as benchmark-independent data.
